.TH scan_ansiskip 3
.SH NAME
scan_ansiskip \- skip an ANSI escape sequence in a string
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <lib/scan.h>

size_t \fBscan_ansiskip\fR(const char *\fIs\fR, size_t \fIlimit\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscan_ansiskip\fR inspects the string \fIs\fR to determine if it begins with
an ANSI escape sequence (starting with the ESC character, 0x1b).
If an ANSI sequence is detected within the first \fIlimit\fR bytes, it calculates
the length of the sequence.

The function recognizes standard CSI (Control Sequence Introducer) sequences
beginning with ESC and '['. It skips over parameters until an alphabetic
character is found, and optionally handles sequences ending with '~'.

.SH RETURN VALUE
\fBscan_ansiskip\fR returns the number of bytes that make up the ANSI escape
sequence. If the string does not begin with an ANSI escape sequence, it returns 0.

.SH SEE ALSO
scan_ulong(3)